# mpv options for Jellyfin MPV Shim. Its libmpv reads this file, not ~/.config/mpv
# or /etc/mpv, and the shim defers to the hwdec set here (media-viewer council
# 2026-11-09). Without VA-API, mpv decodes in software.
hwdec=vaapi
{{- if eq (get .decentangl "machine_id" | default "") "omarchy" }}
# Measured on this laptop (AMD Renoir, on AC): VA-API decodes H.264 and HEVC
# Main/Main10, and dmabuf-wayland hands those frames to Hyprland without a GL pass,
# up to ~0.5 W less than gpu-next. Playback then sits within ~0.5 W of the Chromium
# web app (the web app slightly lower on HEVC) at about a third of its CPU, with no
# server transcode. AV1 (about 1% of the library) has no hardware decoder here: it
# decodes in software, is converted and uploaded through VA-API for display: about
# 0.4 W and ~135% CPU against gpu-next's ~49%, accepted. dmabuf-wayland needs a
# VA-API device and a dmabuf-capable Wayland compositor (without them video fails
# outright) and skips mpv's own tone mapping (the compositor maps PQ instead). HDR10
# (24 of ~3300 items) was checked on one dark frame here: comparable to gpu-next,
# slightly darker shadows; bright highlights not checked. Other hosts keep mpv's
# default gpu-next until measured.
vo=dmabuf-wayland
{{- end }}
# mpv-mpris cannot load into the shim's libmpv (undefined mpv_* symbols), so media
# keys wait for the shim's own MPRIS in 3.2+.
